<DocsLayout
  title="Multi-vault architecture"
  description="Personal hub, project vaults, reference vaults. The privacy boundary is the schema."
  current="multi-vault"
>
  <p>
    Think OS has one personal hub vault, zero-or-more project vaults shared
    via git, and zero-or-more reference vaults that are read-only.
    Privacy is enforced <em>structurally</em> — a project vault's schema has
    no slot for personal content, so the agent cannot write your work log
    into a shared repo because there is no destination.
  </p>

  <h2>Three types</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Personal hub</strong> — your individual knowledge. Identity,
      current focus, work log, decisions, learnings, people. Lives on disk,
      never shared. Always loaded into every agent session.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Project vault</strong> — shared with teammates via git. Reduced
      schema: project home, team activity (one file per entry, append-only),
      decisions (ADR-style, immutable), specs, learnings, roster. No personal
      slots.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Reference vault</strong> — a folder of someone else's markdown
      you want indexed for search. Marked <code>[reference]</code> in agent
      output. Read-only.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Vault registry</h2>
  <p>
    <code>~/.thinkos/vaults.json</code> lists all registered vaults with their
    type, label, path, and Basic Memory project name. Managed via the
    <code>thinkos vault</code> CLI or <code>/thinkos-vault</code> slash command —
    never edited by hand.
  </p>

  <h2>Active-vault resolution</h2>
  <p>
    The agent decides which vault is "active" in this order:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Sticky override at <code>~/.thinkos/active-vault</code> (set by <code>thinkos vault use &lt;id&gt;</code>).</li>
    <li>CWD-derived — if <code>pwd</code> is inside a registered vault path.</li>
    <li>The vault marked <code>default: true</code> (always the personal hub).</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Full design</h2>
  <p>
    The complete architecture, including planned encryption tiers, schema
    enforcement, and the future <code>thinkos vault import-existing</code>
    flow for layering Think OS over a team's pre-existing repo:
    <a href="https://github.com/dhirajsapkal/think-os/blob/main/docs/multi-vault-architecture.md">
      docs/multi-vault-architecture.md
    </a>.
  </p>

  <p class="text-muted text-sm mt-12">
    Rendered docs coming soon. For now, the source files in the repo are authoritative.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
